# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: Exception.new("exc") constructor; throw/catch with isA() guard; re-throw;
#         bare throw; nested try; finally-before-throw; Exception display.
# blocked: Exception structured-throw wiring (defer-v1.x)
# matrix-row: exceptions-try-catch
#
# Reason:
#   isA() shipped at v0.10.11 (Cluster #17 ratify).  Remaining block is
#   Exception structured-throw wiring (defer-v1.x): `catch (var e if
#   e.isA(exc))` requires typed Exception instances, but the runtime
#   currently throws diagnostic strings rather than allocating Exception
#   proto instances.  The typed exception hierarchy (Exception.Constness,
#   Exception.BadInteger, etc.) and the struct-throw wiring that connects
#   OP_THROW to allocate-and-populate an Exception proto are both deferred
#   to v1.x.  isA() itself works correctly post-v0.10.11.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when Exception structured-throw lands):
# # var exc = Exception.new("exc"); [00000001] Exception `exc'
# # throw exc; [00000002:error] !!! input.u:@.1-9: exc
# # try { echo("before"); throw exc; echo("after") } catch(var e if e.isA(exc)) { echo("caught") };
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/exceptions/exceptions.chk)
